  "deviations": [
    "Removed from the page for the comparison because the board omits them: the short case name field, the instructing firm field, and the example hints under text fields (the data and the API need them).",
    "Removed from the artboard because the app has no data for them: the records tile's second line ('GP record, hospital notes, letters') and the court-track hint.",
    "Each drop tile is one big file chooser (its label is visually hidden but stays in the page); the board's inline 'choose files' link has no equivalent.",
    "The claim-against answer is a text box (the board draws a chip with Edit); the report due date is a date field (the board shows typed text); the dictation footer also says 'Your words only' and the Dictate button has no microphone icon.",
    "Court tracks and patient states come from the jurisdiction (mock: Multi-track and Unsure; Living, Has died, Under 18), so their words differ from the board's.",
    "Segmented options and link actions keep a 52px tap area through a transparent ::after; the visible size is the board's.",
    "The footer stays pinned to the bottom of the window (sticky), the board draws it at the end of the page."
  ],
  "pageRemove": [
    ".av-setup-form .av-field:has(input[name=label])",
    ".av-setup-form .av-field:has(input[name=firm_0])",
    ".av-setup-form .av-field__hint"
  ],
  "artboardCss": " main > section:nth-of-type(2) > div:nth-child(6) > div:nth-child(2) > span:last-child { display: none !important } main > section:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-child(2) > span:last-child > br, main > section:nth-of-type(1) > div:nth-child(2) > span:last-child > span { display: none !important }",
  "budget": 1.2,
  "budgetReason": "Words that come from the pack or the app differ from the board's sample copy (the claim-against prompt, 'Jointly instructed', the anything-else hint, the date shown as a date field instead of typed text) and the claim-against answer is a text box where the board draws a chip with Edit; every box on the page is measured by the probes."
